  "construction": "Five original mathematical zones and four CC0 recorded attack zones. Piano uses upright recordings; the ensemble combines trumpet, horn and violin sections with a tuned foundation. Soft Air has no vowel formants, struck rings or fast AM. No legacy LA bank or reference-video audio is used.",
  "sample_rate": 16000,
  "families": 7,
  "peak_target": 26000,
  "guard_frames": 1280,
  "measurement": "centroid_hz and bright_fraction use Hann-windowed FFT frames: a 256-sample attack frame at offset 0, then 1024-sample frames at offset 0, length/4 and the tail. bright_fraction is the share of spectral energy at or above the fourth partial. occupied_bands counts quarter-octave bands from the fundamental up to 7 kHz that stay within 30 dB of the strongest band. stage_rebound is the largest energy climb over a preceding dip in 64-sample blocks across the first 1024 samples, so a staged attack exceeds 1.0 and a single decaying click does not. loop_motion_db is the spread of 256-sample block RMS inside the loop and loop_centroid_range_hz the extremes of six circularly read 256-sample centroids there; both are zero for a frozen loop.",
